~ start
You: We all know mutiny is brewing aboard the ship once again.
Lisa Stone: Captain, I don't have any proof this time, but we all know what kind of person Marley is.
Marley Mildred: Excuse you?!? I have a heart of gold thank you very much. Unlike our old pal Charles. If that man had a heart of gold, he would've sold it. I don't miss him the slightest.
Lisa Stone: See? It be things like that which give you your reputation Marley. Joking about a man who walked the plank not even a day ago!
Marley Mildred: Defending a traitor? Captain PLEASE tell me you're hearing this. Not to mention, we're pirates! You're known across the seas for your fatal tactics and yet you draw the line at jokes about a traitor?
John S. Hark: Dude, don't yell at her for having a little heart.
Marley Mildred: Oh yeah I forgot you were on this crew. Why are you a shark? Has no one thought to ask this? Everyone's mad at me for lying every now and then when we have a literal talking shark on board! How do we know you won't just eat all of us one day?
Lisa Stone: Leave him alone. He may be a shark, but he's more of a man than you'll ever dream of being Marley.
Marley Mildred: Whatever. Hey Bob, you've been awfully quiet don't you think?
Bob Bellows: Mmh
Marley Mildred: So Cap'n? Who do you pick to walk the plank?
=> END